From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hollitizz <valentin.caure@epitech.eu>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 15:27:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ios: compile the host and the iOS front end for the tvOS SDK

The tvOS SDK marks APIs the iPhone front end uses as unavailable, so nothing built for an Apple TV.
Guard them out on TARGET_OS_TV, leaving iOS unchanged: sigaltstack (crash.c, main.m), the volume's
important-usage capacity (hle_svc.c, -1 as when the query fails), WebKit (web_apple.m: the weak
defaults of hle_web.c answer), CoreMotion, haptics, hover and multitouch (DmGamepad.m, whose touch
controls stay hidden), orientation masks and rotation (DmLayout.h, DmRotation.h, front_ios.m, main.m),
screen brightness, the scene accessory, delivered notifications and the Home button setting.
The same guards as seedds/nxnative#868, carried over to the code at the pin.

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: the iOS front end and host built for the tvOS SDK, for Apple TV builds (the guards of the open seedds/nxnative#868, at the pin)
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#85

---
